# Shell scripts run through Git Bash on the Windows runner, where CRLF line
# endings make the interpreter fail on the first line. Pin them to LF whatever
# platform checks them out.
*.sh text eol=lf
# `git apply` matches context bytes exactly: a CRLF-materialized patch never
# applies to Dawn (its .gitattributes pins sources to LF), so patches must stay
# LF on every host, Windows runners included.
*.patch text eol=lf
